2 CONT
2 CONT [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bernhard_Karlgren  '''Klas Bernhard Johannes Karlgren'''] (15 October 1889 – 20 October 1978) was a Swedish sinologist and linguist who pioneered the study of Chinese historical phonology using modern
2 CONC  comparative methods. In the early 1900s, Karlgren conducted large surveys of a number of Chinese dialects and studied historical information on rhyming in ancient Chinese poetry, then used them to create the first ever complete r
2 CONC econstructions of what is now called Middle Chinese and Old Chinese. .  .   .  . 
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bernhard_Karlgren  ''continued]
