1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Her father was Bonde at Bäck 1, like his father and pioneer-grandfather (all ancestors). She inherited the ranch, which in turn went to her eldest son Lars (1723-85). Her brother was lost in war with Russia in Will
2 CONC manstrand, Finland, 1741.
2 CONT She is shown at Sjulsmark 1, Bygdeå (1746-62),  A1:2.15 (1762-72), as Karin with son Lars M. at Umeå and Karin's 2 daughters Lisabeta M. b. 1727 and Margarita M. Karin went on to live with her eldest son Per Mosesson, until her de
2 CONC ath. Shown with son Pehr M., his wife Anna O., and grandkids at Sjulsmark 2, Bygdeå, A1:3.89 (1762-72). Karin died 1766-03-08 at Sjulsmark, Bygdeå, age 80 years, ålderdomskrämpor (old age infirmaties).
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources:
2 CONT Agneta Olofsson, "Bygdeå byar och gårdar 1600 - 1800 " (1999), p. 114, Sjulsmark 2 quotes DII:1.5,17v (1726-1753); Dombok entries.
2 CONT Kurt Andersson, https://www.qhurth.com/anor/0001/38760.htm
2 CONT Kråken 24 database person 104687, https://kråken.se/ shows "A.Olofsson" as birth and death source; HFL Sjulsmark, Bygdeå, AI:2.15 (1746-62) widow b. 1690.
